.env
*.log
__pycache__/
*.zip
*:Zone.Identifier

# Created/reused by scripts/test-grading-api.sh -- test-only deps (pytest,
# httpx), never part of the shipped grading-api image.
docker/grading-api/.venv-test/
# Created/reused by scripts/test-guacamole-e2e.sh -- test-only deps
# (playwright, pytest), never part of any shipped image.
docker/guacamole/tests/.venv-test/
.pytest_cache/

# Claude Code /export transcripts -- these capture the full conversation,
# including any real credentials pasted into chat along the way (e.g. the
# Kasm API key/secret used earlier in this project). Never commit these.
session.md
/*.txt

# Fetched by scripts/fetch-public-samples.sh — not committed, re-fetched from
# Orthanc's public demo server on demand (see that script's own comments).
# The small pydicom fixtures directly under sample-data/ ARE committed.
/sample-data/brainix/

# A real, multi-hundred-slice CT study (970 instances, ~494MB) from
# dicomlibrary.com's own public "DICOM Samples" gallery — confirmed
# anonymized directly via pydicom tags before use (PatientName
# "Anonymized^^", PatientID "0", no institution/physician/accession) --
# not scriptable like brainix/ above: dicomlibrary.com's download link is
# a per-visit, 5-minute-expiring token tied to a "manage" session, not a
# stable public URL. See scripts/fetch-public-samples.sh's own comment
# for how to re-fetch it if this copy is ever lost.
/sample-data/dicomlibrary_ct/

# Local-only radiologist testing guide -- will eventually name the actual
# server address, deliberately kept out of the public repo. See
# docs/LOCAL_SETUP_GUIDE.md (committed) for the developer-facing equivalent.
/PRZEWODNIK_TESTY_LOKALNY.md

# PM's private correspondence (email exports, Teams chat exports) -- never
# committed to this public repo. The root-only /*.txt rule above doesn't
# reach these since they live under Dokumentacja/; this closes that gap
# explicitly rather than relying on remembering not to `git add` them.
Dokumentacja/Marlena_*
Dokumentacja/*.docx

# Both of these were committed on this repo's very first commit, before
# this project had any gitignore discipline at all, and stayed publicly
# exposed on GitHub for ~2 weeks before being caught and purged from
# history (git-filter-repo + a force-push, 2026-09-22). Explicit rules
# here, not just "remember not to git add them": AI_context_Documentation_DICOM.txt
# turned out to be contaminated with scraped, unrelated content (Reddit-
# style comment threads, stray AI-tool UI text) mixed into otherwise
# legitimate project documentation; DICOM_Q&A.txt contains internal cost
# estimates and procurement/legal risk commentary not meant to be public.
Dokumentacja/AI_context_Documentation_DICOM.txt
Dokumentacja/DICOM_Q&A.txt
